Relavia downstream patch 0001: honor the tls-version-max profile
directive in the pinned OpenVPN 3 core (0c1ce172).

Upstream deliberately leaves the OpenSSL context's
tls_version_max field unsettable from a profile ("use for
testing only (NOT exposed via tls-version-max)" —
openvpn/openssl/ssl/sslctx.hpp) and lists the directive among
the ignored options ("We don't allow restricting max
version" — openvpn/client/cliopt.hpp). The apply side already
exists (SSL_CTX_set_max_proto_version); only the parse side
is missing.

Relavia needs the cap for VPN Gate pool sessions: SoftEther's
OpenVPN clone captures the client certificate reliably only
in a classic <= TLS 1.2 handshake on the affected builds, and
answers AUTH_FAILED under TLS 1.3 (diagnosis
docs/真机连接失败诊断-2026-11-14.md §10). The cap itself is
applied per-profile by the Go render layer, keyed to pool
provenance only (core/openvpn/genconfig.go
isVPNGatePoolNode); this patch merely makes the core honor
the standard directive.

Changes (OpenSSL backend only; our builds never compile the
mbedTLS backend):
  - openvpn/ssl/tlsver.hpp: parse_tls_version_max(), mirroring
    the existing parse_tls_version_min() OptionList overload.
  - openvpn/openssl/ssl/sslctx.hpp: parse the directive into
    the existing tls_version_max config field.
  - openvpn/client/cliopt.hpp: drop "tls-version-max" from
    the ignored-with-warning set (it is honored now, so
    reporting it as ignored would be false).

Applied by android/openvpn3/build-openvpn3-android.sh and
android/openvpn3/rig/run-rig.sh right after the pinned
checkout. Rebase cost on a future pin bump: re-check the
three anchors; the patch is intentionally minimal.
